Marqo NSFW Image Detection 384 — model weights
==============================================

The `group1-shard*of6.bin` files in this directory are the weights of

    Marqo/nsfw-image-detection-384
    https://huggingface.co/Marqo/nsfw-image-detection-384

a `vit_tiny_patch16_384` fine-tune published by Marqo under the
**Apache License, Version 2.0**:

    https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

IMPORTANT: these files are NOT covered by `data/LICENSE` (MIT), which applies
to the blocklist and whitelist data in this repository. They remain under
Apache-2.0, and that license travels with them.

They were produced from the upstream Hugging Face weights by
`tools/convert_vit384.py` in this repository. The conversion is a format change
only — safetensors to a TensorFlow.js GraphModel — with no retraining and no
modification of the learned parameters. Verified numerically: the converted
graph reproduces the original model's logits to within 8.3e-7.

Why they live here rather than in the extension package: the BlockNSFW
extension fetches them on first use and caches them locally, so the ~22 MB is
paid only by users who opt into the Vision Transformer classifier, not by
everyone who installs the extension. The matching graph topology
(`models/vit384/model.json`) does ship in the package.

The accompanying graph topology is served from the extension itself; only these
numeric weight files are served from this directory, via
`VIT384_WEIGHTS_BASE_URL` in `shared/ai-image-models.js`. If these files are
ever re-published, bump `VIT384_WEIGHTS_VERSION` in that same file — it is part
of the client-side cache key, and without a bump clients keep serving the old
weights from cache indefinitely.

See also THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in the repository root.
